1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:11,664
95 to 100 percent of homes heating with oil, propane or electricity, and already
running air conditioning, would pay less with a heat pump, a national study estimates.

2
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:20,255
Estimates, because it is a model: the study simulated those
homes' bills, so the figure is not a reading from anyone's meter.

3
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:29,095
Its median saving, $300 to $650 a year, is for those
same homes and moves with the heat pump's efficiency.

4
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:37,612
Drop the air conditioning and the same model is
weaker: only 73 to 86 percent come out ahead.

5
00:00:38,633 --> 00:00:43,361
Whether metered homes agree with the
model is the subject of the full inquiry.
